  "summary": "Four documents directly apply contrastive learning (representation learning with paired positive and negative examples) to battery remaining life estimation, making them the primary candidates. [V0095] evaluates on GridWatch achieving accuracy 0.75 (Chen et al., 2019). [V0094] evaluates on ToxiBench achieving F1=0.68 (Brennan et al., 2018). [V0093] evaluates on CellLife achieving AUROC 0.61 (Adebayo et al., 2026). [V0096] evaluates on ProtMap achieving MAE 0.82 (Duarte et al., 2020). A fifth document, [V0084], applies decentralised training (not contrastive learning) to battery remaining life on ProtMap with AUROC 0.84 (Adebayo et al., 2026); it is included as the closest remaining battery-health study, though its method does not match the contrastive learning criterion. Documents addressing other topics (hate speech, septic deterioration, road traffic, customer attrition) or other methods (self-attention, boosted trees, message passing, multilevel probabilistic models) applied to battery health are excluded as not directly relevant.",
